Teach gnulib's relocatable.c how to find a shared library on QNX.

find_shared_library_fullname() is implemented only for Linux and Cygwin,
both by scanning /proc/self/maps.  QNX has no such file in that format, so
on QNX the function compiles to nothing, get_shared_library_fullname()
always returns NULL, and relocate() hands every path straight back.

That failure is silent and total: enchant dlopens its spell-checking
providers from a directory it composes from the configure-time PKGLIBDIR,
so with --enable-relocatable in effect but relocation not working, a
broker installed anywhere other than the configured prefix constructs
successfully and reports no providers at all.

dladdr() answers exactly the question the /proc scan is asking -- which
object contains this address -- and QNX 8.0 has it in libc, with Dl_info
exposed under __EXT_UNIX_MISC (which _QNX_SOURCE turns on).

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/libgnu/relocatable.c
+++ b/libgnu/relocatable.c
@@ -399,10 +399,27 @@
 
 #else /* Unix */
 
+#if defined __QNX__
+# include <dlfcn.h>
+#endif
+
 static void
 find_shared_library_fullname ()
 {
-#if (defined __linux__ && (__GLIBC__ >= 2 || defined __UCLIBC__)) || defined __CYGWIN__
+#if defined __QNX__
+  /* QNX has no /proc/self/maps in the Linux format, so the scan below cannot
+     work here and a shared library built --enable-relocatable would silently
+     never relocate: every path it composes from the configured prefix stays
+     absolute, and a library that dlopens its own plugins (enchant does, from
+     $libdir/enchant-2) finds nothing once the tree is installed anywhere but
+     the configure-time prefix.  dladdr() answers the same question directly
+     and is in QNX's libc; ask it for the object containing this very
+     function.  */
+  Dl_info info;
+  if (dladdr ((void *) &find_shared_library_fullname, &info) != 0
+      && info.dli_fname != NULL && info.dli_fname[0] == '/')
+    shared_library_fullname = strdup (info.dli_fname);
+#elif (defined __linux__ && (__GLIBC__ >= 2 || defined __UCLIBC__)) || defined __CYGWIN__
   /* Linux has /proc/self/maps. glibc 2 and uClibc have the getline()
      function.
      Cygwin >= 1.5 has /proc/self/maps and the getline() function too.
